From 889236af92bca431fc494820af36e4d4b64dacac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:37:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(4leaf): place battle dice and scores where battle.jpg
 draws them

Measured relative to the original winBattle-01 podium sprite, which a
template match places at (220,265) in the archived 800x600 battle.jpg
(median |diff| 21, 61% exact pixels). In source pixels from the sprite edge:

  anchor              battle.jpg   before   after
  left dice centre        24.0      77.0     24.0
  right dice centre      273.5     278.0    273.5
  dice top (white)        75       105       75
  left score centre       62.0      76.5     62.5
  right score centre     285.0     278.0    285.0
  score top (white)     -153      -160     -153

The original draws the LEFT dice and score left of the left deck; the live
duel centred them. Also: numerals overlap by 7.5 px and dice pairs sit 5 px
apart as in battle.jpg. Offsets are multiplied by a new
--leaf-native-podium-scale variable so they follow the drawn sprite.
Desktop (>=651 px) only; the phone layout is unchanged.

tests/battle-anchor-compare.cjs reproduces battle.jpg's left dice (4, 1)
and requires all six anchors within 3 source px (currently <= 0.9).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
